<% content_for :preview_title, "Reversal shortfall — gift card ##{@gift_card.id}" %>
<% content_for :preheader do %>A merchant reversal created <%= @amount_formatted %> of adjustment balance on gift card #<%= @gift_card.id %>.<% end %>

<div style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:1.2px; text-transform:uppercase; color:#E08A00; margin-bottom:14px;">
  Internal alert · Reversal
</div>

<h1 style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:24px; line-height:1.2; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-0.6px; color:#0D2F32;">
  ⚠️ Reversal could not return all cents to their original load
</h1>

<p style="margin:0 0 20px 0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#2C3A43;">
  A merchant reversed a redemption, but the load(s) it debited had been refunded or
  written off in the meantime. An <code>admin_adjustment</code> load was created on the
  card for the shortfall — the only path that creates balance out of order. Review it.
</p>

<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse; background:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #F1E2CB; border-radius:12px; margin:0 0 24px 0;">
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 16px; border-bottom:1px solid #F1E2CB; font-size:14px; color:#0D2F32; font-weight:700;">Gift card:</td><td style="padding:10px 16px; border-bottom:1px solid #F1E2CB; font-size:14px; color:#2C3A43;">#<%= @gift_card.id %> (<%= @gift_card.merchant&.store_name %>)</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 16px; border-bottom:1px solid #F1E2CB; font-size:14px; color:#0D2F32; font-weight:700;">Reversal transaction:</td><td style="padding:10px 16px; border-bottom:1px solid #F1E2CB; font-size:14px; color:#2C3A43;">#<%= @reversal_transaction_id %></td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 16px; font-size:14px; color:#0D2F32; font-weight:700;">Shortfall:</td><td style="padding:10px 16px; font-size:14px; color:#2C3A43;"><%= @amount_formatted %></td></tr>
</table>
